# Binary
cloop
cloop.exe

# cloop state
.cloop/

# Go
*.test
*.out
vendor/

# A separate project that happens to live here.
#
# polyauth/ is its own Go module (github.com/blechschmidt/polyauth) with no
# .git of its own, so to this repository it looks like 191 MB of untracked
# files — including two built binaries. Unignored, the `git add -A` in the
# standing commit instructions would vacuum an unrelated project into cloop's
# history, where removing it again means a rewrite. Ignoring it is not a
# judgement about the code; it is a fence between two projects sharing a
# directory.
polyauth/

# Documentation site: the staged tree, the rendered site and the pinned venv
# `make docs-site` builds. All of it is derived from docs/ and website/.
dist/

# Terraform working state under deploy/terraform/.
#
# .terraform/ is a downloaded provider cache — hundreds of megabytes of
# platform-specific binary. The lock file is excluded too, which is the
# opposite of the advice for a root module and right for this one: these are
# reusable modules and examples, and a committed lock would pin every consumer
# to whatever provider build resolved on the day it was written.
#
# *.tfstate is the one that matters. A state file here would contain the
# cloop hub's client secret in plaintext.
**/.terraform/
**/.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
crash.log

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
